{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.terminal_defect","record":{"id":"support.terminal_defect","kind":"claim","label":"Square-root terminal deficit on a finite plateau","status":"unverified","source_id":"support_tex_variation","locator":"variation.tex:144–207; eq:terminal-layer; ContactPotential.lean:124–208","statement":"For gamma in U with gamma=c on (a,1), where 0<=a<1 and finite c>=0, and its controlled diffusion, there are C>0 and t0<1 such that 1-q(t)>=C*sqrt(1-t) for t0<t<1. The tilted heat kernel (ordinary heat kernel for c=0) supplies a uniform positive density bound near x=0 at late times; both terminal signs retain positive tilted probability on |x|<=sqrt(1-t).","assumption_ids":[],"evidence_ids":["support_source_bindings_20261024","support_graph_semantic_review_pending"],"citation_ids":["support_terminal_source","support_terminal_defect_lean_source"],"boundary":"Curated source-level mathematical statement, not an elaborated Lean extraction or independently accepted proof. Its displayed local hypotheses are quantified guards; a hypothetical plateau is not an added premise of the full-support theorem. The boundary-layer estimate itself does not use minimality. It uses the finite plateau and terminal cusp, not a derivative estimate uniform up to time 1. Constants depend on the fixed coefficient/plateau; no quantitative bound uniform over minimizers is claimed."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.terminal_defect","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/69473417dc487cafa5e2e39b3168d2c4a8bffdad2e91b6e486de48f122dda071","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]},{"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json/support/0.